{"name":"Doc Layout","description":"Combine section navigation, article content, and an on-page outline · A documentation layout often uses a left navigation for pages, a readable center column for the article, and a right outline for headings. Keep each column's job distinct and collapse secondary navigation on small screens. Know first Sidebar Anchor","quote":"Lay this out like documentation: navigation on the left, the article in the middle, and this page's outline on the right.","agentPrompt":"Implement a three-column docs layout: cross-page navigation left, constrained article center, and current-page anchors right. Hide the outline first on tablets and move site navigation into a mobile drawer. Verify page and section highlights stay distinct.","html":"<div class=\"detail-body detail-entry-doc-layout\"><section class=\"detail-hero\" id=\"detail-hero\"><div class=\"dh-head\"><h1>Doc Layout</h1></div><div class=\"dh-quote\"><span class=\"dh-quote-label\">You might say</span><p class=\"dh-quote-text\">Lay this out like documentation: navigation on the left, the article in the middle, and this page&#x27;s outline on the right.</p></div><div class=\"dh-tagline\"><strong class=\"dh-summary-lead\">Combine section navigation, article content, and an on-page outline</strong><span class=\"dh-summary-separator\" aria-hidden=\"true\">·</span><span>A documentation layout often uses a left navigation for pages, a readable center column for the article, and a right outline for headings. Keep each column&#x27;s job distinct and collapse secondary navigation on small screens.</span><div class=\"prerequisite-row\" aria-label=\"Know first\"><span class=\"prerequisite-label\">Know first</span><div class=\"prerequisite-links\"><a class=\"c-ref c-link\" href=\"/vibe-hub/sidebar-layout?lang=en\" data-ref=\"sidebar-layout\">Sidebar</a><a class=\"c-ref c-link\" href=\"/vibe-hub/anchor?lang=en\" data-ref=\"anchor\">Anchor</a></div></div></div><div class=\"dh-demo responsive-detail-demo